cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Distributed Systems Playground in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Distributed Systems Playground"
abstract: "A browser-based environment for distributed algorithms: they are written in event-driven pseudocode, run on a simulated network whose timing and faults are configured separately from the assumptions of the algorithm, and checked against properties declared next to the code — in a single run or over hundreds of runs with randomly generated faults, summarized as a profile of the conditions the algorithm survives. Eighteen algorithms are included, from reliable broadcast to Paxos and Ben-Or, together with a command line tool for continuous integration."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Del Re"
    given-names: "Francesco"
repository-code: "https://github.com/engineering87/distributed-systems-playground"
url: "https://engineering87.github.io/distributed-systems-playground/"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - distributed systems
  - distributed algorithms
  - simulation
  - education
  - failure detectors
  - consensus
  - fault injection
  - property checking
  - Paxos
  - quorum systems
